      <h2>Form of government</h2>
      <p>
        Osprey Point operates under a Faulkner Act council–manager charter adopted in
        1974. Residents elect a Mayor at large and four Council Members by district to
        staggered four-year terms in non-partisan elections. The Council sets policy,
        adopts the budget, and passes ordinances; the Town Manager, appointed by the
        Council, runs daily operations and supervises department directors.
      </p>

      <h2>When the Council meets</h2>
      <p>
        The Council holds a regular legislative session on the <strong>third Tuesday</strong>
        of each month at 7:00 p.m. in Council Chambers, and a work session on the
        <strong>first Tuesday</strong> at 6:00 p.m. Work sessions are for discussion only;
        no votes are taken.
      </p>
      <p>
        Meetings are open to the public and streamed. As the state Open Public Meetings
        Act requires, agendas are posted at least 48 hours in advance and the town files
        an annual notice of its regular schedule. Draft minutes go up within five business
        days of approval.
      </p>

      <h2>Speaking at a meeting</h2>
      <p>
        Every regular session includes a public comment period near the top of the agenda.
        Speakers get three minutes each and the period runs 30 minutes total. Sign up with
        the Clerk before the meeting is called to order, or email the Clerk by 4:00 p.m.
        that day to be added to the list.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may also submit written comment at any time. Comments received before noon on
        the meeting day are distributed to all members and entered into the record.
      </p>

      <h2>Boards and commissions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Planning Commission</strong> — second Tuesday, 7:00 p.m.</li>
        <li><strong>Board of Appeals</strong> — fourth Wednesday, as needed</li>
        <li><strong>Ethics Commission</strong> — quarterly</li>
        <li><strong>Parks &amp; Open Space Advisory Board</strong> — first Thursday</li>
        <li><strong>Bay Restoration Task Force</strong> — monthly through 2027</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Seven board seats are open as of August 2026. Residents may apply through the Town
        Clerk; appointments are made by the Mayor with Council confirmation.
      </p>

      <h2>Ordinances and the charter</h2>
      <p>
        The town charter and the codified ordinances are maintained by the Town Clerk.
        Ordinances adopted since the last codification are available as individual
        documents from the Clerk's office.
      </p>
